7	// page's own applyTranslations(): a browser decides whether to offer a
8	// translation from the document it received. A page that arrives in English
9	// and becomes Hebrew a moment later is offered the wrong translation, and a
10	// crawler that is served a different language per request has one URL to index
11	// for four languages. Both are answered by shipping each language as its own
12	// document, already in that language.
